/-!
# Rank-one component and parabolic reductions

The preliminary disjunction yields 15.3.26(1), with the genuine `S₃`
quotient and prime-to-three residual. Its consequences bound all
three-subgroups of `M ∩ I` by order three. Once the component is relatively
normal, the centre calculation excludes both even-parameter `SL₃` and
the quasisimple triple cover of A₆. The intersection identities distinguish
`(M ∩ L)*` from its extension by `S*` in the eventual eight-letter marking.

The relative-normality and containment proofs, and the exhaustive marked
alternatives of 15.3.28 including the A₇ exclusion, remain to be assembled.
`MiddleNodePermutationMarking` specifies an output, not its existence.
The minimal-outside clause is already proved in the imported `Basic`
module after containment and the common Sylow witness.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
15.3.26–28, printed pp.1130–1131 (PDF pp.1147–1148).
-/
